From 2bca2126768a95dd2b42ad6cba896bbf40840823 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:24:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Offer our camera in a call that started without it

In a call that started as a voice call, the camera button did nothing:
our answers had said we would not send video, and the plug-in only
waited for the far side to offer again.

Do what teams.live.com does when its camera is turned on mid-call
(captured 2026-11-05): POST an offer of our own, video sendrecv on the
call's media with the same ICE credentials and key, to the far side's
mediaRenegotiation link. That link comes from the callee's acceptance
in a call we placed, and from the acknowledgement of our accept in a
call we answered. The offer names the call's media leg and a
negotiationTag of our participant id and a counter, as the web client's
does. The far side's answer comes as a mediaAnswer frame; it is
acknowledged and its direction starts our camera. An offer with no
answer is given up after 15 s, so the button can try again.

test_needs_offer covers when an offer is made and the tag's shape.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/EionRobb/purple-teams/pull/99]
